nly CL1. And record/ has a CL1 record. Fine \u2014 base green, and we don't change README except status version.\n\nHmm, but careful: count.py also checks for each record in record/: if name matches custody-vX.Y.Z.json and X != version \u2192 continue (skip). So older records skipped. Records not matching that name pattern? e.g. \"custody-v0.9.3.json\" matches. Fine.\n\nAlso count.py checks `if level and f\"claims {level}\" not in readme` for the *current-version* record only... whatever, base green.\n\nAnother count.py check: \"kept record added to record/ carries its release's version in its name\" \u2014 base green.\n\nAnother: quickstart drift \u2014 README quickstart commands vs ci.yml; base green; we don't change those lines. Careful: README's Quickstart block must stay identical.\n\nAnother: `checkers = len([f for f in checker/*.py if f.name != \"__init__.py\"])` \u2014 and SPEC/README must claim that count: \"One reference checker exists\" \u2192 1. Fine, we don't change.\n\nAnother: LICENSE checks \u2014 unchanged.\n\nAnother: `for path in current + schema`: current = md files excluding record/ and CHANGELOG.md. Tokens must equal version. GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, NOTICE, PATENTS.md \u2014 base green means they have no 0.x tokens. Good.\n\nAnother: SPEC header date non-future \u2713; changelog newest = version \u2713.\n\nAnother: record problem: \"release 0.9.9 has no record/custody-v0.9.9.json and no record/RECORD-GAP-v0.9.9.md saying why\" \u2192 exactly one problem. And measure_count_except_record requires parts[\"record\"] non-empty (matching regex with version 0.9.9) and stale/rest empty.\n\nCareful about count.py gap check: any record/RECORD-GAP-v*.md whose version not in GAP_EXCEPTIONS \u2192 problem. v0.9.8 is in the exception \u2192 fine.\n\nNow also count.py checks `want` enums match schema/checker, and `missing = [v for v in want[key] if f\"`{v}`\" not in spec and v not in spec]` \u2014 unchanged.\n\nNow, the CHANGELOG: newest version heading m