r. Avoid lines like `**artifact** |`.\n\nAlso \"one home\" check: `re.search(rf\"^\\s*[|*-]*\\s*\\*\\*{re.escape(t)}\\*\\*\\s*[|:\u2014-]\", text, flags=re.M|re.I)`. So a line starting (after optional decorations) with `**bar**` followed by `|`, `:`, `\u2014`, `-`. Avoid bolding terms at line start.\n\nAlso count.py `sizes`: normative words <= 4500 etc. \u2014 unchanged SPEC normative text, fine. Checker line lengths \u2014 frozen.\n\nNow the DRAFT-NOTE target from plumbline presumably has a specific shape. I'll craft a sensible one.\n\nLet me now also double check test_06's plant that inserts the amendment: \n\n```\nwith_rule = self._edit(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\", lambda t: t.replace(\n    \"At most one release a month while the version starts with 0\",\n    \"At most one release a month while the version starts with 0; \" + CADENCE_AMENDMENT, 1))\nself.assertEqual([p for p in measure_cadence(with_rule) if \"amendment\" in p], [])\n```\n\nSo the inserted amendment must be inside `## Releases` section, and measure_cadence must not complain about the amendment. Our real CONTRIBUTING must already contain the amendment (for test_06's subject check `measure_cadence(self.subject) == []`).\n\nSo Releases section:\n\n```\n## Releases\n\nAt most one release a month while the version starts with 0, quarterly after 1.0. Versions follow\nSemantic Versioning 2.0.0; `SPEC.md` section 8 says what counts as a major change. Every release is a\ngit tag, and is cited by its commit. A release that changes no requirement does not count toward the\nmonthly cadence.\n```\n\nWait \u2014 the CADENCE_AMENDMENT is exactly \"a release that changes no requirement does not count toward the monthly cadence\" (lowercase 'a'). carried_verbatim compares `needle in \" \".join(haystack.split())` \u2014 case-sensitive substring. So we must include the sentence with lowercase \"a\"? If our sentence starts \"A release that changes...\" then the needle \"a release that changes...\" is a substring of it? \"A r