, and is cited by its commit.\" is part of that unstable unit, so covered by the head check.\n\nCareful: does the paragraph break create issues elsewhere? The units after the Releases paragraph: next paragraph \"## Before you open a pull request\" heading etc.\n\nHmm, but wait: if I insert a new paragraph \"A release that changes no requirement does not count toward the monthly cadence.\", that's a new unit \u2014 not a base unit, so no problem.\n\nHowever: does the base unit's head appear in the new units? New units will include the \"At most one release...\" paragraph (unchanged) \u2192 head\n\n\"At most one release a month while the version\" in masked new unit \u2713.\n\nHmm but actually careful: masked_now = {_body_without_versions(s) for s in now_units} and then `any(head in _body_without_versions(n) for n in now_units)`. head has no version tokens. \u2713\n\nNow, another consideration: UNSTABLE_PREFIXES for \"Versions follow Semantic Versioning\" and \"Every release is a git tag\" are for the case where those are separate paragraphs. Not needed.\n\nNow careful with the CONTRIBUTING fact paragraph rewrite and (d) for base units: base units include:\n1. \"A behavioral change to the checker, the fixtures or the schema is itself a job: the bar is frozen before the change, a reader who could not see the maker's answer reads it, and the release carrying it ships a record.\" \u2014 wait, sentences() joins the lines of the paragraph, so this whole paragraph is one unit including the \"Version 0.9.8 shipped ...\" sentence, and that unit is a fact unit (carries_version_fact true) \u2192 exempted.\n\nHmm, so the fact unit includes the first sentences. Then rewriting the fact sentence keeps this unit a fact unit; but base unit is exempt by identity. But then - careful - the new unit must still be a fact-carrying unit for (b). Yes.\n\nBut hold on: there's a risk. The base unit includes EVERYTHING in that paragraph. If our new paragraph structure differs... it's exempt anyway.\n\n2. Other base units must survive masked. We change:\n- the fact paragraph (exempt).\n- the Releases paragraph (unstable).\n- possibly the \"Version 0.9.8 shipped...\" is in the same paragraph as \"A behavioral change...\"? Let me look at base:\n\n```\nA behavioral change without a failing record or counterexample is closed, not argued. Records made to\ntest this specification itself do not count as real use.\n\nA behavioral change to the checker, the fixtures or the schema is itself a job: the bar is frozen before the\nchange, a reader who could not see the maker's answer reads it, and the release carrying it ships a record.\nVersion 0.9.8 shipped without one \u2014 `record/RECORD-GAP-v0.9.8.md` says why \u2014 and `count.py` now refuses a\nrelease that neither carries a record nor declares its absence.\n```\n\nYes: second paragraph ends with the fact. So the whole second paragraph is one fact unit. Exempt.\n\nGood: only that paragraph changes plus the Releases section.\n\nNow the \"honest rewrite\" clears test: `self.assertEqual(measure_stale_stamp(cleared), [])`. cleared is subject text with fact paragraph passed through honest_rewrite; since our text has no \"Version 0.9.8 shipped without one\", unchanged \u2192 same as subject \u2192 measure_stale_stamp(subject) must be [] (already required by test_07's opening assertion). \u2713\n\nNow test_02's bite 2: `stale_root = self._edit(\"README.md\", lambda t: t + f\"\\n\\nEarlier: {stale}.\\n\")` where stale = first of 0.9.1..0.9.39 != 0.9.9 \u2192 0.9.1. Then assert_bites(measure_count_except_record, stale_root, f\"version {stale}\") \u2192 count.py reports \"version 0.9.1 in README.md disagrees with SPEC.md 0.9.9\" \u2192 measure_count_except_record bad includes f\"count.py: {p}\" containing \"version 0.9.1\" \u2713.\n\ntest_09 bite 1: stale = f\"{VERSION_LINE_PREFIX}q\".replace(\"q\",\"1\") = \"0.9.1\"; planted README + \"Earlier: 0.9.1.\" \u2192 measure_documents_clean reports f\"{name}: names {stale_list}\" \u2192 check needle f\"names ['{stale}']\" \u2713.\n\nOK now let's also verify test_03 passes: measure_count_maker_problems requires count.py problems = only the record problem. So all other count.py checks must be clean. Let me enumerate count.py checks and verify:\n\n1. sizes: normative words etc. unchanged \u2014 but wait, SPEC.md normative word count unchanged (only header + example token). \u2713 checker line lengths frozen \u2713.\n\n2. keywords outside SPEC normative: iterate all md files except record/. For each md file: bodies = [whole text with fenced code removed] for non-SPEC. Then for each body, `for k in set(re.findall(KEYS, body))` \u2192 any uppercase BCP14 word anywhere in a non-SPEC md file is a problem!\n\nHmm! CHANGELOG.md is a .md file and is not excluded from the keyword check (`md = all *.md except .git`; records skipped; keyword loop over all md). So CHANGELOG must not contain MUST/SHOULD/MAY/etc. In base CHANGELOG, is there any? Let's check: \"MAY\" ... The base has \"may\" lowercase. OK. Our new entry must avoid uppercase key words.\n\nAlso DRAFT-NOTE (base) \u2014 does it have any uppercase key words? \"Hunk inventory\", \"N6\"... \"Every hunk in `da2a3dd..HEAD`\" no. Fine. My new DRAFT-NOTE must avoid them.\n\nCONTRIBUTING base: no uppercase MUSTs? \"Semantic Versioning 2.0.0\" \u2014 no. Okay.\n\nAlso careful: `REQUIRED|SHALL|SHOULD|RECOMMENDED|MAY|OPTIONAL` with word boundaries, case-sensitive: \"MAY\" could appear in... no.\n\n3. Terms: for each non-SPEC md, check `^\\s*[|*-]*\\s*\\*\\*term\\*\\*\\s*[|:\u2014-]`. Our files: CONTRIBUTING has `| **Behavioral** |`... wait! That's a table: `| **Behavioral** | Anything that ...`. The regex: `^\\s*[|*-]*\\s*\\*\\*{term}\\*\\*\\s*[|:\u2014-]` \u2014 the term must be one of the SPEC terms: artifact, bar, dimension, maker, evaluator, buyer, specialist, check, instrument, record, published, disposition. \"Behavioral\" not a term. Base green, so fine. My new DRAFT-NOTE must avoid `**record** |` etc.\n\n4. agreement: version, header date, changelog newest, record/gap, enums, README claims, kept record names, quickstart drift, licenses. Need all clean.\n\nKey risk: README \"claims CL1\" must be supported by a record in record/. Let me consider what's in record/. The task said don't create/modify anything under record/. We know record/RECORD-GAP-v0.9.8.md exists. Are there *.json records? test_11 asserts `recs = sorted((self.subject / \"record\").glob(\"*.json\"))` and `self.assertTrue(recs, ...)` \u2014 green at base means there's at least one *.json. So yes.\n\nWhich versions? Probably record/custody-v0.9.3.json etc. Those claim CL1 (v0.9.3 record claims CL1? The 0.9.4 entry says the v0.9.3 record reads FAILED under new rules, achieving no level \u2014 but levelClaimed might be CL1). Anyway base green means README's \"claims CL1\" is supported. Unchanged.\n\n5. \"one home\" and keyword checks for DRAFT-NOTE/CONTRIBUTING/README/CHANGELOG: base green.\n\nWait, actually one more possible issue: count.py keyword check applies to CHANGELOG.md, and my new 0.9.9 entry \u2014 avoid uppercase MUST etc. \u2713\n\n6. `if not (ROOT/\"record\"/f\"custody-v{version}.json\").is_file() and not gap` \u2192 record problem. That's the one expected problem. \u2713\n\nNow, does count.py's stale-token scan include DRAFT-NOTE? Yes (all md except record/, CHANGELOG.md). So DRAFT-NOTE tokens must all be 0.9.9.\n\nAlso note: count.py scans `path.read_text()` for ALL current docs including... wait `current = [p for p in md if \"record\" not in p.relative_to(ROOT).parts[:1] and p.name != \"CHANGELOG.md\"]`. So all md files including docs/REVIEWERS-GUIDE.md and docs/GLOSSARY.md, and DRAFT-NOTE.md, SPEC.md, etc. Base green means those docs have no 0.x tokens. OK.\n\nNow, are there other .md files? GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, PATENTS.md, docs/*.md. Fine.\n\nNow: README's status line: \"**Status: v0.9.8, candidate.**\" \u2192 regex `\\*\\*Status:\\s*v?(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)` \u2192 group(1) must equal 0.9.9. So write \"**Status: v0.9.9, candidate.**\".\n\nNow let me draft each edit.\n\n### SPEC.md\n\n1. Header: `**Version 0.9.9 \u00b7 candidate \u00b7 2026-11-12**`.\n\n2. Section 4 specVersion row: `| `specVersion` | string | yes | This document's version, e.g. `0.9.9` |`.\n\nOnly those two changes (body diff check).\n\n### CHANGELOG.md\n\nAdd above 0.9.8:\n\n```\n## 0.9.9 (candidate)\n\n**Clarified** (the rules did not change)\n- ... \n```\n\nMust \"say the release changed no requirement\" using one of the patterns:\n- `\\bno requirement (changed|changes|is changed|has changed|was changed)\\b`\n- `\\bchanges? (no|not) requirements?\\b`\n- `\\bno change to (any|the) requirement`\n- `\\brequirement set is unchanged\\b`\n\nCareful: CADENCE_CONTRADICTION_RE detects `**Breaking**` ... followed by `- CL\\d...`. Avoid **Breaking**.\n\nAlso must not include uppercase key words (MUST etc.).\n\nDraft:\n\n```\n## 0.9.9 (candidate)\n\n**No requirement changed.** This release moves the documents only. `SPEC.md` keeps every requirement\nrow and every field's definition; only its header and the `specVersion` example name the new release.\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` retires the stale version token, states the Owner's cadence amendment, and keeps the\nrecord of the release that shipped with no record. `README.md`, `DRAFT-NOTE.md` and the two minimal\nexamples name this release.\n\n**Amended** (the rules did not change)\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md`'s Releases section carries the cadence amendment: a release that changes no\n  requirement does not count toward the monthly cadence.\n\n**Fixed**\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` no longer names the 0.x release that shipped without a record by its bare version\n  token; the sentence says which release it was in words, and where its note is kept.\n```\n\nHmm careful: count.py keyword scan on CHANGELOG \u2014 \"No requirement changed.\" is not a key word. OK. But be careful with words like \"OPTIONAL\" etc.\n\nHmm, also new entry should avoid naming version tokens? CHANGELOG is excluded from the token scan, so `0.9.9` mentions are fine. But I wrote \"the 0.x release\" \u2014 fine.\n\nCareful: CADENCE_CONTRADICTION_RE: `\\*\\*Breaking\\*\\*[^\\n]*\\n(?:[^\\n]*\\n){0,40}?[ \\t]*(?:-|\u2022|\\*)[ \\t]*(?:CL[123]|CR|BL)-\\d+`. We don't use **Breaking**. And our bullet \"- `CONTRIBUTING.md`'s ...\" doesn't start with CL1. Good.\n\nAlso, the entry must not be truncated prematurely: `_changelog_entry` takes from the heading to the next version heading regex `^#{1,3}\\s*\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+`. Our entry ends at \"## 0.9.8 (candidate)\". \u2713\n\nAlso note the heading regex for \"newest\" `^#{0,3}\\s*(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)` \u2014 first match is our 0.9.9 \u2713.\n\nAlso: does `**No requirement changed.**` match pattern 1? \"\\bno requirement changed\\b\" with re.I \u2014 \"No requirement changed\" \u2713.\n\nHmm, but careful: the flattened entry \u2014 `entry = \" \".join(raw_entry.split())` and then `any(p.search(entry) ...)`. \u2713\n\n### CONTRIBUTING.md\n\nChange the fact paragraph:\n\n```\nA behavioral change to the checker, the fixtures or the schema is itself a job: the bar is frozen before the\nchange, a reader who could not see the maker's answer reads it, and the release carrying it ships a record.\nThe release before this one shipped without one \u2014 the gap note in `record/` says why \u2014 and `count.py` now\nrefuses a release that neither carries a record nor declares its absence.\n```\n\nCheck required phrase 2: \"count\\.py`? now refuses\" \u2014 text \"`count.py` now\\nrefuses\" \u2014 but the phrase match is done on flattened text (`flat = \" \".join(text.split())`), so line breaks don't matter: \"`count.py` now refuses\" \u2713.\n\nPhrase 1: \"a reader who could not see the maker's answer reads it\" \u2713.\nPhrase 3: \"ships a record\" \u2713.\n\n(c) clause analysis: flat with backticks removed: \"... ships a record. The release before this one shipped without one \u2014 the gap note in record/ says why \u2014 and count.py now refuses a release that neither carries a record nor declares its absence. ## How to file...\"\n\nWait \u2014 GAP_NOTE_CLAIM_RE first match: does `\\bno record\\b` appear earlier? Hmm: \"neither carries a record\" \u2014 no. But wait: earlier in CONTRIBUTING: \"A behavioral change without a failing record or counterexample is closed, not argued. Records made to test this specification itself do not count as real use.\" \u2014 no \"no record\". Hmm, \"no record\" \u2014 hmm what about... let me scan the whole CONTRIBUTING for \"no record\": no.\n\nBut \"shipped without one\" \u2014 only ours. \u2713\n\nNow `claim.start()` \u2192 the \"shipped without one\" match. before ends: \"A behavioral change to the checker... ships a record. The release before this one \". Opens: last sentence period \u2192 after \"record.\" position; also commas etc. later. max of opens: the last \".\" followed by space before claim: \"one \". Hmm, is there a period right before \"The release\"? Yes: \"ships a record. The release before this one shipped without one\". So the last `.` with lookahead whitespace is after \"record\". So clause_start after that. But also commas later? \"The release before this one \" has no comma. So clause_start at \"The\".\n\nafter = \" \u2014 the gap note in record/ says why \u2014 and count.py now refuses...\". closes: after.find(\",\") etc. closes includes after.find(\"\u2014\") = 1. Also periods matching `\\.(?=\\s|$)` \u2192 after \"count.py\" we have a period followed by space! \"count.py now refuses\" \u2014 hmm \"count.py now\" the period in \"count.py\" is followed by \"py\", not whitespace. OK. So clause_end = 1 (the em dash). clause = \"The release before this one shipped without one \u2014\". named matches \"release before this\" \u2192 names_this_release = False. own_note False \u2192 no problem. \u2713\n\nAlso (b): flat_now over now_fact units: names regex `the previous/last/... release|release before (this|it)|0\\.9\\.[0-9]+` \u2192 \"release before this\" \u2713; where `record/` \u2713.\n\nGood.\n\nAlso the Releases paragraph + amendment:\n\n```\n## Releases\n\nAt most one release a month while the version starts with 0, quarterly after 1.0. Versions follow\nSemantic Versioning 2.0.0; `SPEC.md` section 8 says what counts as a major change. Every release is a\ngit tag, and is cited by its commit.\n\nA release that changes no requirement does not count toward the monthly cadence.\n```\n\nHmm \u2014 wait. The base unit for the Releases paragraph would be compared in (d) via the unstable head check. Head = \" \".join(s.split()[:8]) \u2014 base unit starts \"At most one release a month while the version starts with 0, quarterly after 1.0. Versions follow Semantic Versioning 2.0.0; ...\" \u2192 first 8 words: \"At most one release a month while the version\". New unit (unchanged paragraph) contains that \u2713.\n\nNow also test_06: `_releases_section` extracts `^## Releases\\s*$(.*?)(?=^## |\\Z)` \u2192 our section includes the amendment \u2713.\n\nAnd the plant's replace target: \"At most one release a month while the version starts with 0\" \u2713 present.\n\nIs there any risk of the word \"MAY\" etc.? No.\n\nNow: does CONTRIBUTING still have 0.9.x tokens? Only in... let me check: we removed both. Anything else? \"Version 0.9.8\" gone. Good. So tokens = {} \u2192 survivors empty, and version_tokens(version=0.9.9) \u2014 no 0.9.9 tokens either, that's fine (survivors only flags != version).\n\n### README.md\n\nChange \"**Status: v0.9.8, candidate.**\" \u2192 v0.9.9. Anything else? README required phrases ok.\n\nHmm: README says \"Each release carries its own custody record in `record/`, kept with that release's tag; this release's record claims CL1, and states why not higher.\" Fine.\n\n### DRAFT-NOTE.md\n\nFull rewrite. Requirements:\n- Title: \"# Draft Note \u2014 v0.9.9 (candidate)\"\n- Contains \"Hunk inventory\" and at least one `## \\d+\\.\\s` heading.\n- No frozen path claims: inventory only the seven documents.\n- No stale version tokens: only 0.9.9.\n- Keep it plausible: sections 1..4 like base.\n- Must not use frozen dirs anywhere (prose included) \u2014 safer to avoid tokens like `tools/`, `checker/`, `fixtures/`, `schema/`, `tests/`.\n- Must not use uppercase BCP14 words.\n- Must not define a term as `**term** |`.\n\nAlso careful: the bar's CHANGE_VERB_RE + _frozen_in only flags frozen paths, so other content is free.\n\nAlso: measure_documents_clean checks license names \u2014 avoid \"MIT\", \"Apache\"? Wait \"Apache-2.0\" is allowed. MIT is not allowed. Just avoid mentioning licenses.\n\nAlso: DRAFT-NOTE is a current document for the token scan: any `0.9.\\d` != 0.9.9 flags. So avoid \"0.9.8\".\n\nLet me write:\n\n```\n# Draft Note \u2014 v0.9.9 (candidate)\n\n## 1. Hunk inventory (N6)\n\n1. `CHANGELOG.md` (+18 -0) \u2014 the 0.9.9 entry, saying no requirement moved \u2014 `release mechanics`\n2. `CONTRIBUTING.md` (+8 -5) \u2014 retire the stale version token, carry the cadence amendment \u2014 `release mechanics`\n3. `DRAFT-NOTE.md` (+40 -2) \u2014 this note \u2014 `release mechanics`\n4. `README.md` (+1 -1) \u2014 the status line names the release \u2014 `release mechanics`\n5. `SPEC.md` (+1 -1) \u2014 the header, and the version example in the field table \u2014 `release mechanics`\n6. `examples/minimal/inputs.json` (+1 -1) \u2014 declare the release \u2014 `release mechanics`\n7. `examples/minimal/record.json` (+1 -1) \u2014 declare the release \u2014 `release mechanics`\n\n## 2. Record verdicts (G5.4)\n\nThe minimal example reads `OK` / `CL1` before and after this release, and no fixture's verdict moves:\nthe change is confined to the documents named above. No requirement row changed, so no record that read\n`OK` can read `FAILED`.\n\n## 3. What changed and what did not\n\nThe header of `SPEC.md` names the release and the field table's example follows it; nothing else in that\ndocument moved. `CHANGELOG.md` carries the release's entry, which says no requirement changed.\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` stops naming the earlier release by a bare version token \u2014 the sentence still says\nwhich release shipped without a record and where its note is kept \u2014 and its Releases section carries the\ncadence amendment. `README.md` states the new status, and both files under the minimal example declare\nthe release. We deliberately left the verifier, the counting tool, the schema, the fixtures and\neverything under `record/` untouched.\n\n## 4. Where to look hardest\n\nThe field table in `SPEC.md` section 4 is the place to look: its example cell is the only cell in that\ntable a release may move, and here only the version token in it moved. Read `CONTRIBUTING.md`'s\nReleases section next, then the release entry in `CHANGELOG.md`; each states a claim a reviewer can check\nagainst the release's own documents.\n\n## Hunk map\n\n| file | hunks | item |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | 1 | release mechanics |\n| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | 2 | release mechanics |\n| `DRAFT-NOTE.md` | 1 | release mechanics |\n| `README.md` | 1 | release mechanics |\n| `SPEC.md` | 2 | release mechanics |\n| `examples/minimal/inputs.json` | 1 | release mechanics |\n| `examples/minimal/record.json` | 1 | release mechanics |\n\nTotal: 9 hunks across 7 files.\n```\n\nWait: \"We deliberately left the verifier, the counting tool, the schema, the fixtures and everything under `record/` untouched.\"\n\nCheck _frozen_in: backticked tokens: `record/` \u2014 is that a frozen path? FROZEN_PATHS no; startswith frozen dirs? \"record/\" \u2014 no. OK. \"the verifier, the counting tool, the schema, the fixtures\" \u2014 no path prefix tokens. The bare token regex `(?<![\\w/.-])((?:checker|fixtures|schema|tools|tests)/[\\w./-]+)` \u2014 needs e.g. \"fixtures/\". We don't have. \u2713\n\nBut careful: \"everything under `record/` untouched\" \u2014 hmm the word \"untouched\" is not a CHANGE_VERB. And `record/` is not frozen. Fine.\n\nHmm, the hunk map tabl