tains \"**Breaking** (what a producer must change)\" \u2014 lowercase must. Fine.\n\nNow, potential gotcha: my new CHANGELOG entry contains \"`SPEC.md` keeps every requirement row and every field's definition\" \u2014 fine.\n\nLet me also double check the CADENCE_CLAIM_PATTERNS don't accidentally match... we need a match. \"No requirement changed.\" \u2713.\n\nHmm, but caution: pattern 2 `\\bchanges? (no|not) requirements?\\b` \u2014 no. Pattern 1 matches.\n\nNow, is there a risk that `CADENCE_CONTRADICTION_RE` matches within our entry? It needs literal \"**Breaking**\". Not present \u2713.\n\nLet me also make sure the entry includes a real heading format: \"## 0.9.9 (candidate)\" \u2014 `^#{0,3}\\s*(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)` \u2713.\n\nLet me write the CHANGELOG block carefully with a SEARCH on the \"# Changelog\" header + first lines.\n\nBase:\n```\n# Changelog\n\nEach release is a git tag, and each carries its own custody record in `record/`, or a note in `record/` saying\nwhy it does not. Before 1.0.0 any release may turn a record that read `OK` into one that reads `FAILED`\n(SPEC.md section 8); every such change is listed here under **Breaking**.\n\n## 0.9.8 (candidate)\n```\n\nI'll insert the new section between.\n\nAlso should I mention that this release changes no requirement... yes done.\n\nNow: \"each carries its own custody record in `record/`, or a note in `record/` saying why it does not.\" Hmm \u2014 for 0.9.9 there's no record yet (that's Instrument 2). This sentence in the changelog preamble is pre-existing; fine (CHANGELOG is not token-checked nor content-checked).\n\nHmm, but careful with count.py keyword check over CHANGELOG: the preamble has \"may\" lowercase.\n\nNow writing the blocks.\n\nLet me write the DRAFT-NOTE carefully avoiding uppercase BCP14 key words: check my text: \"MAY\"? no. \"MUST\"? no. \"REQUIRED\"? no. \"SHALL\"? no. \"SHOULD\"? no. \"RECOMMENDED\"? no. \"OPTIONAL\"? no.\n\nWait, in section 3 I have \"We deliberately left...\" \u201